---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About NoCharge"
  description="About NoCharge: 17 free browser games, complete player guides, browser-local results, practical editorial, and no account requirement."
  path="/about/"
  showAds={false}
>
  <article class="trust-page prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About NoCharge</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">A quiet place for free browser games and practical guides.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        NoCharge is a one-word brand for a library of 17 browser games available at no charge and without an account. It pairs the arcade with complete game guides, focused articles, reviewed collections, and Quiet Setup editorial. Documented results stay on the device where they were played.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-what">
      <h2 id="about-what">What NoCharge is</h2>
      <p>
        NoCharge is a browser-game and guide library. The current arcade catalog holds seventeen games: eleven solo
        titles — Memory Match, Word Tile Rush, Color Flip, Beacon Lattice, Klondike, FreeCell, Nonogram, 2048, Tile
        Garden, Word Search, and Mini Sudoku — and six Pass &amp; Play games for two players on one device, listed in
        full on the <a href="/arcade/">Arcade page</a>. Each title is
        available in the browser without an account, installation, or profile setup.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site’s Quiet Arcade approach favors clear controls, readable pages, practical game information, and
        respectful optional services over noisy interruptions. The point is to make it easy to play a short round,
        understand a rule, and leave when you are done.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-guides">
      <h2 id="about-guides">Games and guide library</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/guides/">guide library</a> documents each live game’s rules, controls, scoring behavior,
        and accessible play options. The <a href="/articles/">article library</a> adds focused examples about a
        single behavior or decision, such as scanning a board or tracing a diagonal letter path. Guides are
        editorial reference material, not a substitute for the game itself or a promise of a result.
      </p>
      <p>
        We update guides and supporting articles when a documented game behavior changes. The{' '}
        <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a> records verified public platform updates.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-accounts">
      <h2 id="about-accounts">No-account and local-data model</h2>
      <p>
        NoCharge does not offer user accounts, passwords, cloud saves, or public scoreboards. Game best scores
        and a few preferences are stored in local browser storage on the device you use. They are not uploaded to
        NoCharge or synchronized between devices. You can clear local game data from the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-accessibility">
      <h2 id="about-accessibility">Accessibility commitment</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to make the site understandable and usable with keyboard, touch, pointer, and assistive technology
        where the games support them. This includes visible focus, meaningful button names, documented controls,
        pause behavior for timed play, Color Flip’s untimed turn-based mode, and Beacon Lattice’s untimed exact-cover
        board with numeric coverage labels. Accessibility is ongoing work;
        please report a barrier so it can be reviewed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-privacy">
      <h2 id="about-privacy">Privacy-first optional services</h2>
      <p>
        Analytics is optional and stays off until a visitor allows it. Advertising is one labeled Google AdSense
        banner at the bottom of eligible pages, with Google&rsquo;s Privacy &amp; messaging consent message managing
        advertising choices and no ads over gameplay. The Privacy page explains those choices, local storage, and
        how to withdraw consent at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="about-operator">
      <h2 id="about-operator">Publisher and contact</h2>
      <p>
        The publisher and operator identity currently available on this site is <strong>NoCharge</strong>. For a
        question, accessibility report, privacy concern, or problematic advertisement report, contact{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@nocharge.net">hello@nocharge.net</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trust-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .trust-page > header {
    padding: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .trust-page section {
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .trust-page section + section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
</style>
